#16. A weather prediction system estimates the probabilities of three possible conditions as sunny, rainy, and cloudy: P=[0.6, 0.3, 0.1]. The system needs to measure the uncertainty in its predictions. Write a Python program to calculate the entropy of the probability distribution and to display the probabilities of the three weather conditions in a bar chart.
import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
from scipy.stats import entropy

P = np.array([0.6, 0.3, 0.1])
H = entropy(P, base=2)

print("Entropy:", H, "bits")

plt.bar(["Sunny", "Rainy", "Cloudy"], P)
plt.ylabel("Probability")
plt.title("Weather Probabilities")
plt.show()
